{"questions":[{"question_id":"eyfVH29R8xCOmcfP","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"rotational-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"combined-translational-and-rotational-motion","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0.75,"permalink":"consider-a-disc-rotating-in-the-horizontal-plane-with-a-cons-2012-marks-3-eyfvh29r8xcomcfp.htm","content":"Consider a disc rotating in the horizontal plane with a constant angular speed <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> about its centre\nO. The disc has a shaded region on one side of the diameter and an unshaded region on the\nother side as shown in the figure. When the disc is in the orientation as shown, two pebbles P\nand Q are simultaneously projected at an angle towards R. The velocity of projection is in the y - z\nplane and is same for both pebbles with respect to the disc. Assume that (i) they land back on\nthe disc before the disc has completed <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.816ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.773ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 793.6 1225.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> rotation, (ii) their range is less than half the disc radius,\nand (iii) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> remains constant throughout. Then<br><br>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l25415rw/2fd36b7e-6400-4e4a-a8ac-0e998f64abe2/bcbfdbc0-bf4d-11ec-b997-87cc5d16a405/file-1l25415rx.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l25415rw/2fd36b7e-6400-4e4a-a8ac-0e998f64abe2/bcbfdbc0-bf4d-11ec-b997-87cc5d16a405/file-1l25415rx.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Rotational Motion Question 71 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l25415rw/2fd36b7e-6400-4e4a-a8ac-0e998f64abe2/bcbfdbc0-bf4d-11ec-b997-87cc5d16a405/file-1l25415rx.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l25415rw/2fd36b7e-6400-4e4a-a8ac-0e998f64abe2/bcbfdbc0-bf4d-11ec-b997-87cc5d16a405/file-1l25415rx.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l25415rw/2fd36b7e-6400-4e4a-a8ac-0e998f64abe2/bcbfdbc0-bf4d-11ec-b997-87cc5d16a405/file-1l25415rx.png?format=png 100